A||N||2||Monkeyman||Removing carpet from door panels???||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||06-22-2001||08:25 PM||||I'm trying to remove the carpet from the lower half of my door panels (going to replace it with vinyl).  The only problem is the glue.  Superman couldn't remove this stuff.  How do I get the carpet off the door??  There must be some trick that I haven't found yet.  Help!<P>MM||||reg||5
Z||000001||Devotshka||06-22-2001||08:53 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>  How do I get the carpet off the door??  There must be some trick that I haven't found yet.  Help!<BR>MM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you aren't saving the carpets, take a can of aerosol paint remover (CitriStrip smells nice   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">) And spray it on the TOP of the carpets.  After about 2-3 minutes it will have soaked through and you will be able to lift the old carpet off with very little effort, starting at the edges (or the armrest hole if the edges don't give up real easily).  Just wipe off the excess, and once the leftover stripping agent has dried, wipe it down so that the new material will stick. I used a touch of lacquer thinner just to be sure it was clean.<p>[This message has been edited by Devotshka (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-22-2001||08:59 PM||||Thanx, Devotshka.  I'll try to find that tomorrow.  I don't care about the carpet.  I plan on covering some thin, dense foam with vinyl then gluing that to the bottom of the door.<P>Thanx, again.<P>MM||||reg||1
